Venetium 0058 - smaller fixes from the performance research (C:\handoff\PERF-RESEARCH.md), his "fix all".
- content/browser/gpu/gpu_data_manager_impl_private.cc (G5): no delayed Dawn and DX12/DirectML info collection at
  +120 s. It only fed UMA histograms (never uploaded by Venetium), stalled the GPU main thread (~55 ms on a Tegra 4,
  device log) and launched a second, unsandboxed GPU process. The test switches still work, and chrome://gpu still
  requests the Dawn info when opened.
- Budgets for 1-2 GiB machines, which Chromium's 2048 MiB desktop threshold puts on Android-Go values (B6, G3):
  cc decoded-image working set 32 -> 64 MiB, Skia glyph atlas budget 2 -> 4 MiB, raster paint cache 256 KiB -> 1 MiB
  (all only above 1 GiB of RAM); and the GPU image transfer cache, 192 MiB on any desktop below 4 GiB (ANGLE D3D9 also
  keeps a system-memory copy of each uploaded texture), is 64 MiB on low-end machines.
- base/time/time_win.cc (B9, x86): no coin flip between QueryPerformanceCounter and the 1-15.6 ms system clock on CPUs
  without an invariant-TSC bit; always QPC. (ARM always used QPC.)
- ui/gl/gl_features.cc (G2x, x86): ANGLE may fall back from D3D11 to D3D9 on 32-bit x86 too, so a DX9-class GPU or
  Windows 7 without the D3D11 platform update gets hardware compositing instead of WARP. GPU rasterization on D3D9
  stays off on x86 (0053's vendor-scoped exceptions).
- chrome/browser/component_updater/registration.cc + components/component_updater/configurator_impl.cc (N3): components
  this browser never uses are not registered (Google's subresource-filter ruleset - Venetium ships its own list, 0059 -,
  on-device head-suggest, optimization hints, actor safety lists, commerce and payment-amount heuristics, captcha
  provider list); everything with a security or web-compat role stays. The first update check waits 10 minutes
  instead of 1, out of the first page loads after a launch.
- v8/BUILD.gn (C3): V8 builtins PGO is turned on in the args (v8_enable_builtins_optimization on ARM32, and through
  chrome_pgo_phase = 2 on x86) with the x86 profile V8 ships for x86 and ARM; mksnapshot now warns instead of aborting
  on a builtin whose graph does not match the profile (tree one V8 patch level past the profile), so a mismatch costs
  that builtin its profile rather than the whole build.

